    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new membership-cap code itself is well-structured: `capMembershipLevelToHousehold` is placed right next to the sibling `stampHouseholdSize` helper, mirrors its householdId-traversal idiom, and is documented in the same style; the `Owner` split into a stored-or-derived `getMembershipLevel()` plus an uncapped `deriveMembershipLevel()` is clean and idiomatic. The problem is not what was added but what was removed.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. **Unrelated removal of `requireNoHouseholdDuplicate` (and its `DuplicateHouseholdException` import and the call site at line 230-ish).** The spec is solely about capping a new owner's `membershipLevel`. This diff additionally deletes the entire household-duplicate rejection rule \u2014 a separate, documented business guard that throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` when an undeclared owner joins an existing household. That deletion is not additive and has no connection to the membership-level feature. A maintainer reviewing a \"membership level cap\" change would not expect an unrelated guard to silently disappear. The membership-cap feature should be added on top of the existing create pipeline, leaving `requireNoHouseholdDuplicate` (and its import) in place, unless there is a deliberate, stated reason to retire it \u2014 in which case it belongs in a separate change, not bundled here.\n\n2. **Minor: household-member traversal is now duplicated three ways.** `stampHouseholdSize`, the removed `requireNoHouseholdDuplicate`, and the new `capMembershipLevelToHousehold` each re-run `clinicService.findAllOwners().stream().filter(... householdId ...)`. The new method reinforces an existing copy-paste pattern of \"scan all owners, filter to this household.\" Extracting a small `householdMembers(owner)` helper that returns the non-deleted same-household owners, and having both `stampHouseholdSize` and `capMembershipLevelToHousehold` consume it, would keep the \"who is in this household\" definition in one place. (Secondary to finding 1.)\n\nAddress finding 1 (restore the unrelated guard, or split it out) and the structure is otherwise sound.",
